## Model card (verified facts only)

- **Name:** LongCat-2.5-Preview (Meituan; "Preview"/free-access wording is part of the launch, not a separate tier)
- **Short description:** Meituan's newest sparse-MoE frontier preview, launched 2026-09-25 with the same advertised scale as LongCat-2.0 (~1.6T total / ~48B active parameters, 1M-token window) plus one genuinely new capability: image understanding. It is positioned for long-horizon agentic work across terminals, browsers, GUIs, spreadsheets and design tools.
- **Provider / access:** LongCat API platform — OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions plus an Anthropic-compatible Messages endpoint; also routed through third-party gateways and available free on OpenCode's Zen/Go list with the same OpenCode API key (no separate signup, unlimited monthly limit under Go, zero-retention stated).
- **Release / knowledge:** Released 2026-09-25; knowledge cutoff not disclosed.
- **IDs:** `meituan/longcat-2.5-preview` (`longcat/longcat-2.5-preview` also accepted); free entry on OpenCode's model list. Existing platform users receive a 5,000,000-token free grant.
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 tokens in, 131,072 max output (LongCat docs/AnyRouter); the quick-start guide describes 128K max output for both 2.5 and 2.0, so the output figure needs confirmation before production use.
- **Modalities:** text, image **and video** input — the 2026-09-25 changelog added image understanding, and a 2026-09-27 setup report confirms **video by public URL only** (MP4, MOV, MKV, AVI, WebM, up to 50 MB and one hour; base64 upload is images-only); text out; a `thinking` toggle that can be enabled or disabled, with the reasoning trace returned inline in an interleaved field. The published chat-completions reference still shows only plain-text message content, so image/video payloads should be tested before relying on them. That 2026-09-27 report also re-confirms the 1M-in / 128K-out shape from Meituan's own quick-start guide — i.e. the 131,072 figure above should be read as 128K output until the vendor restates it.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-09-27):** promo paid-usage rates $0.30 / 1M uncached input, $0.006 / 1M cached input, $1.20 / 1M output (¥2 / ¥0.04 / ¥8) — the vendor labels these discounted and limited-time. **Free** on OpenCode's Zen list with no published end date. Open weights: not announced for 2.5 (LongCat-2.0 was open; that status does not carry over).
- **Architecture:** Mixture-of-Experts, ~1.6T total / ~48B active parameters (~3% active per token), same scale figures Meituan published for LongCat-2.0.

